{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>The hidden things belong to HaShem our Elohim.</b> Because it is written והבדילו ה' לרעה and afterward הדור האחרון, which implies that the entire land would be punished on account of one individual or one family — therefore it is written הנסתרות לה' אלהינו: and He is the judge to exact payment from the doer of evil, to repay him his due, and Israel would not be punished on his account. But the revealed things — the transgressions committed openly — upon us and upon our children the punishment, if we do not eradicate the evil from our midst. And in Sanhedrin it concludes: why are נקודות (dots) on לנו and ולבנינו and on the ע of עד עולם? Because He did not punish for the hidden things until they crossed the Jordan — meaning that then they accepted the Torah as one and became guarantors for one another; then 'the hidden things belong to us and to our children.' And if you ask: if so, since the hidden things are excluded from לה', he should have placed the dot on לה' אלהינו — one may answer that it is not the way of honor to place a dot on the Name, for it would be erased. And since the dot's proper place is on לה' אלהינו, and they transfer it to place it on לנו ולבנינו, therefore the dot is on the ע of עד, to complete. Some say: eleven dotted letters, corresponding to לה', which has eleven letters. And in the Masoretic tradition we learned that the question arises concerning this dot — לנו ולבנינו, what does it come for? And the answer given: thus said Ezra the Scribe when he wrote in the Torah: if Moses our teacher comes and asks, 'Why did you write this?' — he says to him, 'Therefore I dotted over them,' and if he says, 'You wrote well,' I will remove the dot from them. This implies that he was uncertain about the revealed things — whether they apply to 'us and our children' before Israel crossed the Jordan or not — and therefore he dotted over them. And from here there is a slight proof for those who write a verse without lining-out, that they place dots on two words before writing the third, because the dot is like an erasure, since Ezra said, 'Therefore I dotted over them' — and it is as though I did not write them."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:01:39.075517099Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}